  "script": "Who is the 18-year-old kid who just scored 2 goals in 4 minutes for Barcelona? Barcelona just spent 8 and a half million euros on an 18-year-old kid most fans had never even heard of. A winger named Jesse Bisiwu, who was born in Belgium to a family with Ghanaian roots. But the reason Barcelona were willing to gamble that much on a teenager goes back years before this moment. He started playing football at Leuven back in 2014 before moving to Club Brugge in 2020. And at just 15 years old, he signed his first professional contract and started featuring for the development team, making 36 appearances in Belgium's second division, where he scored some bangers. Then at the 2025 Under-17 Euros, he led Belgium to the semifinals and got named in the team of the tournament. But everything he had done up to that point was about to get overshadowed in a single afternoon. Barcelona signed him on a five-year deal and right away he was training with the first team. So against Basel, with Barcelona already ahead, coach Hansi Flick sent him on with about 11 minutes left. In the closing stages, this kid who had never played a single senior game for Brugge scored two goals in the space of two minutes. And even though Lamine Yamal was on that same pitch fresh off winning the World Cup, nobody was talking about Yamal after. They were talking about Jesse.",
